---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import Icon from "../components/Icon.astro";
import { SITE, withBase } from "../lib/blog-data.js";
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`About - ${SITE.name}`}
  description={`About ${SITE.name}: a personal hobby blog collecting and organizing notes on IT and AI.`}
  canonical="/about"
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-12">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: "Home", to: "/" }, { label: "About" }]} />

    <header class="mt-6">
      <div class="text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-primary">About</div>
      <h1 class="mt-2 font-serif text-5xl font-semibold leading-[1.05]">
        Notes on IT &amp; AI, kept by a curious hobbyist.
      </h1>
    </header>

    <div class="prose-article mt-10">
      <p>
        This site is a personal corner of the web &mdash; a hobby project where I collect, organize,
        and rewrite notes about information technology. You'll find write-ups on software,
        systems, tooling, and artificial intelligence that I found interesting enough to keep,
        understand properly, and share.
      </p>
      <p>
        A quick note before you go any further: <strong>I am not a professional writer or a
        formal authority on any of this.</strong> These notes reflect my personal understanding,
        gathered from many sources across the internet and reorganized in my own words. They may
        be incomplete, oversimplified, or occasionally wrong. Treat them as a starting point &mdash;
        and always double-check against the official documentation.
      </p>
      <h2 id="why-this-site-exists">Why this site exists</h2>
      <p>
        I read a lot, and I forget even more. This blog is my way of holding on to the good parts:
        the commands that took too long to figure out, the concepts that finally clicked after the
        third explanation, and the developments in AI worth following. Writing them down helps me
        understand them &mdash; and if they happen to help you too, that's a bonus.
      </p>
      <h2 id="copyright-and-privacy">Copyright &amp; privacy</h2>
      <p>
        Much of the material here is collected from the public internet &mdash; documentation,
        articles, images, and other resources &mdash; then condensed, quoted, or referenced. I do
        my best to credit original sources wherever possible. If you believe anything on this site
        infringes your copyright, or otherwise raises a privacy concern, please get in touch with
        me right away, and I will review and remove it as soon as I can.
      </p>
      <h2 id="lets-talk">Let's talk</h2>
      <p>
        I'm always happy to discuss IT, AI, and anything related &mdash; to exchange ideas, correct
        my mistakes, or swap recommendations. Whether you spotted an error, want to dig deeper into
        a topic, or simply love the same tools I do, don't hesitate to reach out.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="mt-12 border-t border-border pt-10">
      <a
        href={withBase("/contact")}
        class="group inline-flex items-center gap-2 font-serif text-xl font-semibold hover:text-primary"
      >
        Get in touch
        <Icon name="arrow-right" class="h-4 w-4 transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-0.5" />
      </a>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground">
        Questions, corrections, or copyright &amp; privacy concerns &mdash; all welcome through the contact page.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
